      },
      {
        "number": 34,
        "question": "What is the difference between manual sync and automatic sync?",
        "answer": "Manual synchronization requires an authorized user or automation process to request deployment of the desired configuration. Automatic synchronization allows Argo CD to apply eligible changes when it detects differences.\n\nManual sync provides an explicit operational control point, while automatic sync reduces manual deployment work.\n\nFor example, a development environment may use automatic synchronization for faster feedback. A production environment may require manual synchronization after change approval and validation."
      },
      {
        "number": 35,
        "question": "How do you troubleshoot an Argo CD application that is OutOfSync?",
        "answer": "First, inspect the Application status and identify the resources marked OutOfSync. Review the diff between the desired Git configuration and the live Kubernetes resources.\n\nNext, check whether the difference was caused by a recent Git commit, a manual cluster change, a mutating admission controller, or another controller modifying the resource. Verify the configured source revision and destination cluster.\n\nAfter identifying the cause, decide whether Git should be updated or the live resource should be reconciled. Do not blindly synchronize production resources before reviewing the diff and understanding its impact."
