        "answer": "After an upgrade, investigate deprecated or removed APIs, changed admission behavior, incompatible controllers, CSI or CNI add-ons, node AMIs, and application dependencies. Compare the deployment timeline with the cluster upgrade and inspect events, pod logs, controller logs, and API errors. Review Kubernetes release notes and API deprecation warnings from the pre-upgrade assessment. Validate manifests against the target Kubernetes version and check Helm chart and operator compatibility. Confirm node readiness, DNS, networking, storage, and ingress components independently. Roll back an application release or apply a compatible manifest where safe, but do not assume that the managed control plane can simply be downgraded. Establish a tested recovery plan before future upgrades."
