      {
        "number": 36,
        "question": "How do you secure an EKS cluster using Kubernetes RBAC and AWS IAM?",
        "answer": "EKS security combines AWS IAM authentication with Kubernetes authorization and workload-level controls. Use access entries or the supported cluster authentication configuration to map approved IAM principals to cluster access. Apply Kubernetes Roles and RoleBindings for namespace-scoped access and ClusterRoles only when cluster-wide permissions are required. Workloads should use dedicated service accounts with IRSA or EKS Pod Identity rather than static AWS access keys. Restrict access to Secrets, use network policies where appropriate, protect the API endpoint, and review audit logs. Separate human, CI/CD, and workload identities. Test permissions with kubectl auth can-i and periodically review unused or excessive access."
