        "question": "What is the difference between Maven SNAPSHOT and release versions?",
        "answer": "A SNAPSHOT version represents work that is still under development and may be updated as the project changes. Maven repositories can maintain snapshot metadata that maps a logical snapshot version to timestamped artifact files. A release version represents a published version intended to remain stable and should normally be immutable in a production artifact repository. For example, 2.5.0-SNAPSHOT is different from 2.5.0. In CI/CD, publish snapshots to a snapshot repository and approved release versions to a release repository. If consumers receive unexpected content, inspect snapshot metadata, repository policy, caching, and the exact timestamped artifact. Do not overwrite released artifacts as a normal deployment strategy."
