        "answer": "A Jira project is a workspace that organizes related work and defines project-level configuration. An issue is an individual work item. An epic represents a larger body of work that can contain multiple stories or tasks. A story describes a user-focused requirement, while a task represents a unit of work that may be technical or operational. A sub-task breaks a parent issue into smaller activities and normally retains a relationship with that parent. In a DevOps project, an epic might represent a platform migration, stories might cover pipeline improvements, tasks might cover infrastructure changes, and sub-tasks might cover validation steps. Choosing the correct issue type improves reporting, ownership, estimation, and traceability."
