        "question": "Q33. How would you investigate a detached HEAD state in a CI pipeline?",
        "answer": "A detached HEAD means the checkout points directly to a commit rather than a local branch. This is common in CI systems that check out a pull-request or commit SHA for reproducibility. Inspect git status and git rev-parse HEAD to confirm the checked-out revision. If the pipeline must create commits, explicitly create or switch to a named branch based on the intended remote ref. For build-only pipelines, detached HEAD is usually safe and should not be treated as an error."
      },
