        "answer": "Use a supported remote backend with encryption, access controls, versioning or recovery capability, and locking appropriate to the backend. Separate state by environment, application, or ownership boundary to reduce blast radius and contention. Restrict write access to approved automation identities and prevent developers from casually modifying production state. Define backup and recovery procedures, audit state access, and avoid storing secrets in state because sensitive markings do not encrypt the underlying values. Test state recovery and locking behavior before depending on it for critical deployments.",
