        "number": 9,
        "question": "How do you handle Terraform state refactoring when renaming resources or moving them into modules?"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Lifecycle settings influence how Terraform handles resource changes. create_before_destroy can create a replacement before removing the old object when the provider and infrastructure permit it. prevent_destroy blocks planned destruction through Terraform while the rule remains configured. ignore_changes suppresses selected attribute differences during planning, and replace_triggered_by can trigger replacement when referenced objects or attributes change. These options do not eliminate infrastructure constraints or downtime. Use them only when the operational behavior is understood, and inspect the plan to confirm replacement order, naming constraints, capacity requirements, and rollback options.",
        "number": 10,
