      },
      {
        "answer": "Use policy frameworks such as Sentinel, OPA-based tooling, or equivalent plan evaluation to enforce rules before infrastructure changes are approved. Policies can restrict public storage, require encryption, limit regions, enforce tags, and block overly permissive security rules. Evaluate the planned resource values rather than relying only on text searches through configuration. Provide clear failure messages and documented exception workflows. Test policy rules against both compliant and non-compliant plans, version policy bundles, and prevent unauthorized users from bypassing mandatory production checks.",
