        "number": 12,
        "question": "How do you manage secrets and sensitive values in Terraform without exposing them in state or logs?"
      },
      {
        "answer": "A saved plan captures Terraform's proposed actions for a particular configuration, state snapshot, and input set. A CI pipeline can generate a plan, publish it for review, and apply that exact saved plan after approval using the appropriate workflow. Protect plan files because they may contain sensitive values. Ensure that the state has not changed in a way that invalidates the plan and handle stale plans by generating a new one. Record the source commit, workspace, backend, provider versions, reviewer, and apply result. Do not approve plans based only on a short summary when replacements or destructive actions are involved.",
