      {
        "question": "Q31. How do you troubleshoot Terraform dependency cycles?",
        "answer": "A dependency cycle occurs when resources or modules depend on each other directly or indirectly, preventing Terraform from determining a valid creation order. Inspect the cycle reported by Terraform and review references, depends_on declarations, module inputs, and outputs. Remove unnecessary explicit dependencies and redesign resources so ownership and data flow are one-directional. Sometimes separate stages or states are required for foundational infrastructure and dependent services. Run terraform validate and plan after restructuring to confirm the graph is acyclic."
