      {
        "question": "Q2. Compare Jira Cloud and Jira Data Center architecture and explain the operational differences for administrators.",
        "answer": "Jira Cloud is operated by Atlassian as a managed service, so infrastructure maintenance, platform upgrades, and much of the underlying availability engineering are handled by the provider. Jira Data Center is a self-managed deployment in which the organization operates the application nodes, database, shared home, networking, monitoring, backups, and upgrades according to supported architecture. The administrative responsibilities and available customization options differ between deployment models. Before designing integrations or operational procedures, confirm the product edition and version because features, APIs, app compatibility, and infrastructure controls are not identical."
